    "answer": "Seasons and axial tilt: Earth's seasons are caused by the 23.5° tilt of its rotation axis, which changes the directness of sunlight and the length of daylight through the year — not by changes in Earth's distance from the Sun. Seasons come from sun angle and day length changing with the 23.5° axial tilt — Earth is actually closest to the Sun in January. You’ll find this in Lesson 2: Seasons and Axial Tilt, especially in Study Guides, Lesson Plans, Discussion Prompts.",
